  "final_message": "Fixed the inconsistency in `grammar/precedence.ebnf`: since `unary` is level 70 and `exponent` is level 60, unary binds tighter than exponent — so the documented example now reads `unary-binds-before-exponent` (previously it incorrectly stated the opposite). The `unary` and `exponent` production rules themselves were left unchanged.",
